{
  "name": "Tamale Market Monitor",
  "description": "Monitors the Tamale Market Finder app every 6 hours \u2014 checks if the site is live, PWA installability, Supabase connection, security headers, and reports findings to the owner via Telegram.",
  "trigger": {
    "condition": null,
    "config": {
      "trigger_type": "scheduled",
      "events": [],
      "schedule_mode": "recurring",
      "cron_expression": "0 */6 * * *",
      "one_time_date": null,
      "timezone": "Africa/Accra",
      "interval_value": null,
      "interval_unit": null,
      "interval_anchor": null,
      "ends_type": "never",
      "ends_on_date": null,
      "ends_after_count": null
    }
  },
  "definition": {
    "document": {
      "dsl": "1.0.0",
      "name": "tamale_market_monitor",
      "namespace": "base44",
      "version": "2.0"
    },
    "do": [
      {
        "monitor_app": {
          "call": "invoke_superagent_step",
          "then": "end",
          "with": {
            "message": "You are monitoring the Tamale Market Finder app (https://tamale-market-finder.vercel.app). Run these checks and report a concise summary to the owner via broadcast_message:\n\n1. SITE HEALTH: Use curl to fetch https://tamale-market-finder.vercel.app/ \u2014 check HTTP status 200 and that the HTML contains product cards.\n\n2. PWA CHECK: Use curl to fetch /manifest.json and /sw.js \u2014 verify both return 200 and manifest.json has valid JSON with name, icons, and display:standalone.\n\n3. SUPABASE CHECK: curl https://djcajmglxkmhbipmweps.supabase.co/rest/v1/public_shops?select=id&limit=1 with header 'apikey: eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZSIsInJlZiI6ImRqY2FqbWdseGttaGJpcG13ZXBzIiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJpYXQiOjE3ODA4NTE3NDcsImV4cCI6MjA5NjQyNzc0N30.ccaT6pQW8Dbqy1LC97p2hH0Q7CuYtWJwnoDgrOdwAX4' \u2014 verify it returns JSON data.\n\n4. SECURITY HEADERS: curl -I https://tamale-market-finder.vercel.app/ \u2014 verify CSP, X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options, Referrer-Policy headers are present.\n\n5. CONSOLE ERRORS: Navigate to the site with browserbase, take a screenshot, check for visible errors.\n\n6. REPORT: Compose a brief status report. Format: \u2705 or \u274c for each check. If all pass, keep it to 2-3 lines. If issues found, describe them and suggest fixes. Send via broadcast_message."
          },
          "x-base44": {
            "description": "Check site, PWA, Supabase, security headers, console",
            "title": "Monitor app health & PWA"
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}